#! files=20000 dirs=200
# Tier B: searching this folder, over twenty thousand files the index has never seen.
#
# A run has no MFT index, so the first search is a live walk of the disk streaming hits in batches,
# while a background crawl writes the subtree into the scratch database for next time. The later
# searches may be answered from that index — which is exactly what a user gets on an un-indexed
# drive, and why the four are reported separately rather than averaged. Every sample includes the
# 200 ms typing debounce; `search` waits for the query to start before it waits for it to finish.

bench-fixture 20000 200 Deep
go Deep
time search.word search f0012
time search.ext search ext:txt
time search.regex search re:^f001
time search.clear clear-search
assert-count 200
mem search
assert-not-launched
